.TH TRANSUME-CLI 1 "July 2026" "Transume 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
transume-cli \- declarative, safe Transume automation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B transume-cli
.I export|validate|dry-run|execute
.I job.json
.RB [ --resolve-selectors ]
.RB [ --yes ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Validates strict PublicJobSpec JSON without invoking a shell. Input is a regular,
non-symlink file no larger than 1 MiB, or standard input specified as
.BR - .
JSON results are written only to standard output; diagnostics are written to
standard error.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B export
Normalizes a strict PublicJobSpec and writes it to standard output or
.B --output
using an atomic, mode 0600 file replacement.
.TP
.B validate
Checks command construction, runtime binaries and capabilities, repository/image
containment, and current device identities.
.TP
.B dry-run
Runs the same privileged-runner protocol in dry-run mode.
.TP
.B execute
Runs through PolicyKit and requires
.BR --yes .
Encrypted backup and restore jobs cannot be executed by this CLI because their
secret must use the interactive UI secret channel.
.SH SELECTORS
With
.BR --resolve-selectors ,
source and destination entries may each be exactly one of
.BR {"serial":"VALUE"} ,
.BR {"wwn":"VALUE"} ,
.BR {"by_id":"VALUE"} .
The selector must resolve to exactly one current device, which is rebuilt into a
fresh DeviceIdentity. Path-only destructive selectors are rejected.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 2 command-line usage error; 3 invalid input or failed validation; 4
runner failure; 5 execute refused because --yes was not supplied.
